From 1ff6863b04bf715b268e8b2d71acdce22d67b9b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Serhii Nikolaichuk <nikolaichuk.s.f@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 15:38:52 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] attest: a backend that forwards to a deployed Verifier
 and RRPs

internal/tacra is an AttestationCA for the revised EST profile that uses
no mock: attest-initiate asks the RRP serving the Target (a Credential
Authority or Secret Vault gateway) for the Freshness Kind and Handle;
the second leg is correlated with that attest-initiate, the Evidence is
submitted to a Veraison challenge-response session whose nonce is the
binding value computed with the RRP's identifier, and the Attestation
Results go with the request to the RRP, whose answer or refusal (with
its status) is returned. The backend mints no Handle and appraises
nothing. Classic EST enrollment is refused.

The initiation response gains rrp_id. A CA implementing the new
RawRetriever returns the Secret Vault's container unchanged
(the hpke-auth container of the revised profile), and the client's
RetrieveCredentialRaw reads it as sent; the mock's paths are unchanged.
cmd/estserver takes a "tacra" configuration section.
